<template><div class="page"><SiteNav active="qa"/><main><section class="qa-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">QA work / documentation sample</p><h1 class="page-title">AI-CAKE quality assurance <em>case study.</em></h1><p class="intro">Practical manual and technical QA on a role-based cake-ordering system: functional coverage, defect verification, risk reporting, and release-readiness assessment.</p><a class="button primary" :href="base+'documents/ai-cake-qa-testing-portfolio.pdf'" target="_blank">Open full QA portfolio ↗</a></div></section><section class="qa-numbers"><div class="shell"><article><span>01</span><strong>181</strong><p>PHP files syntax-checked</p></article><article><span>02</span><strong>03</strong><p>Role workspaces audited</p></article><article><span>03</span><strong>02</strong><p>Payment paths reviewed</p></article><article><span>04</span><strong>06</strong><p>Verified defects documented</p></article></div></section><section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Test coverage</p><h2>What I tested.</h2></div><p>Coverage combined source inspection, route checks, controlled smoke tests, and cross-role regression.</p></div><div class="testing-grid"><article v-for="(block,index) in coverage" :key="block.title"><span>0{{index+1}}</span><h3>{{block.title}}</h3><ul><li v-for="item in block.items" :key="item">{{item}}</li></ul></article></div></div></section><section class="risk-section"><div class="shell"><div class="risk-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Defect triage</p><h2>Clear about what was fixed — and what needs a release decision.</h2></div><div class="risk-grid"><article class="verified"><span>Verified fixed</span><h3>Six documented defects</h3><p>Authentication routing, staff schedule drill-down, responsive account actions, chat hierarchy, unified role login, and account-specific cart handling.</p></article><article class="risk"><span>Open release risk</span><h3>Payment and deployment hardening</h3><p